1
00:00:00,150 --> 00:00:01,142
There's a side of the Moon

2
00:00:01,142 --> 00:00:02,440
you will never see from Earth!

3
00:00:02,440 --> 00:00:02,920
Why?

4
00:00:03,120 --> 00:00:04,400
You might think it doesn't spin

5
00:00:04,400 --> 00:00:05,687
but the Moon really does spin

6
00:00:05,687 --> 00:00:07,385
once every 27 days or so

7
00:00:07,585 --> 00:00:09,004
That's exactly the same time

8
00:00:09,004 --> 00:00:10,192
it takes to circle Earth

9
00:00:10,192 --> 00:00:11,424
So with every step forward

10
00:00:11,424 --> 00:00:12,847
it turns a little toward us

11
00:00:13,047 --> 00:00:14,750
The cause? Earth's gravity

12
00:00:14,750 --> 00:00:16,254
tugged on it for millions of years

13
00:00:16,254 --> 00:00:18,058
until its spin slowed and locked

14
00:00:18,258 --> 00:00:19,577
And the far side isn't dark

15
00:00:19,577 --> 00:00:20,883
the Sun lights it up too

16
00:00:21,083 --> 00:00:23,065
It spins, yet always faces us

17
00:00:23,065 --> 00:00:24,606
so you'll never see its other side!
